@startuml
title M-SH2 - Controller recovery and controlled restart (SH2+ target)
actor "Initiating caller / optional board\ncaller account" as Caller
participant "swarma-session-host\nservice account / replacement controller" as Host
database "Host-private metadata, fences, epochs\ntranscripts, receipts, inbox, goal revisions\nowner: host" as State
participant "swarma-dispatcher\nexecution / capacity record owner" as Dispatcher
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot-owned generation ledger / exec.stop" as Manager
participant "swarma-user-launcher\nroot until UID/GID change" as Launcher
participant "swarma-session-runner\nworker-<label>; transport + lease owner" as Runner
participant "Harness / private Codex app-server\nworker-<label>" as Harness
participant "swarma-credential-broker\nCodex auth-owner refresh" as Broker

note over Host,Broker
  Target only: joint ticket / host-role / runner-channel activation (§3.3, §7).
  Dispatcher v0 refuses interactive/resume; user-manager signed grants are v2.
  Current / SH1: tb-sessiond owns PTY/app-server; Claude dies on replacement.
end note

== Controller failure while execution may still live ==
Host -> State : reconcile durable fence / controller epoch before effects
note over Host,Runner : Nothing writes to runner before reconciliation (§3.4).
Host -> Dispatcher : recover: distinguish controller, runner, execution and unknown evidence
alt Live authenticated runner confirmed
  Runner <-> Host : re-authenticate / reconnect to replacement controller
  Host -> State : verified controller-only re-adoption under current epoch
  note over Host,Runner
    Keep execution ID; rotate execution-scoped authority on replacement.
    Account generation, execution ID, ticket epoch and controller epoch are distinct.
    Reconnect channel and wire: unspecified in spec §7.
    FD3 carries only plan; no extra inherited descriptor assumed.
  end note
else Execution confirmed absent
  Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : absence permits capacity release / cleanup / replacement
else Unknown or unreadable execution evidence
  Host -> State : keep fence closed / evidence unknown
  Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : keep capacity owned; no replacement or cleanup
end

== Separate scenario: authorised controlled restart (§3.5), only fence holder ==
note over Host,Runner : Controller-only re-adoption above does not itself require an execution restart.
Caller -> Host : authorised restart / explicit recovery
Host -> State : hold delivery closed; invalidate pending interactions
Host -> Runner : drain external effects and child tools
note over Host,Runner
  Bounded note attempt may use marked snapshot fallback.
  Timeout never proves drain; explicit stop has no automatic restart.
  Drain protocol / failure disposition: unspecified in spec §3.5.
end note
Host -> Dispatcher : request execution stop
Dispatcher -> Manager : exec.stop (owned generation / execution)
Manager -> Manager : verify receipt / process identity; TERM then KILL if needed
alt Process absence unresolved
  Manager -> Manager : absence unconfirmed; no successful stop return
  Host -> State : remain fenced; no replacement
  Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : retain capacity
else Process absence confirmed
  Manager --> Dispatcher : confirmed execution absence
  Host -> Host : confirm native-lock absence
  alt Native-lock evidence unresolved
    Host -> State : remain fenced; no replacement / reopening
    note over Host,Dispatcher : Unknown admission permits stay owned (§3.4).
  else Native-lock absence confirmed
  Host -> Host : check binding, posture, authentication, grants, runtime
  alt Native resume requested with violated preconditions
    Host --> Caller : refuse incompatible version / family / home / profile / digest / lock / auth / grants / transport
  else Supported recovery row and current authority
    note over Host,Harness
      Native resume: same machine, same major (0.x same minor),
      same runtime family / home / profile pin, intact transcript digest,
      exclusive native lock, ready auth and current grants; preserve transport.
      Unsupported recovery rows stay visibly parked or refused.
    end note
    Host -> Dispatcher : newly admitted execution; new execution ID
    Dispatcher --> Host : ticket bound to generation, execution, ticket epoch, executor, plan digest, expiry
    Host -> Manager : redeem once for authenticated host
    alt Wrong principal / replay / altered plan or executor / expired or revoked claim
      Manager --> Host : refuse; no new start
    else Valid ticket and live claim
      Manager -> Launcher : journal redemption / launch intent / receipt atomically
      Launcher -> Launcher : validate generation, executor and home; reset environment/descriptors
      Launcher -> Launcher : atomic start receipt; clear groups; set GID/UID
      Launcher -> Runner : exec approved runner; FD3 immutable plan only
      Runner -> Broker : open broker connection after UID change (broker-mode Codex)
      Runner -> Harness : initialise / native resume under closed host fence
      alt Harness native resume fails
        Runner --> Host : resume-failed
        Host --> Caller : resume-failed; caller decides next action
        note over Host,Harness : No automatic fallback or portable seed on native resume.
      else Readiness unknown or re-authentication needed
        Runner --> Host : unknown readiness / authentication not ready
        Host -> State : park; keep delivery closed
      else Admitted readiness reported
        Runner --> Host : readiness / replayable start and readiness receipts
        Host -> State : reconcile dispatched input marker against intact transcript
        alt Matching marker
          Host -> State : receipt applied; no duplicate delivery
          Host -> State : reopen only after restart checks and reconciliation
        else Confirmed marker absence in intact transcript (ordinary input)
          Host -> State : redelivery permitted; reopen after reconciliation
          Host -> Runner : redeliver at turn boundary, same sender/message identity and op_id
          note over Host,Runner : This ordinary-input branch never auto-replays an unknown approval or control effect.
        else Unresolved evidence
          Host -> State : unknown; keep fence closed
          note over Host,Runner : Unknown approval answer / control effect never auto-replays.
        end
      end
    end
  end
  end
end

note over Host,Manager
  Lost launch reply: resolve same effect ID and receipt, never a second start.
  Cancel/redemption interlock, signature bytes and acknowledgement-crash protocol:
  unspecified in spec §3.3 / §7; publish and test before activation.
end note
